      { q: "Why does the lesson call her a ‘rare beam of light’?", options: ["She lit the path for women in science despite barriers","She worked with lights","She invented a lamp","She studied the sun"], answer: 0, explain: "She succeeded in a field dominated by men.", level: 3 },
      { q: "Why is the legacy of Bibha described as still unfinished?", options: ["She discovered everything","No women are left in science","Women still face challenges","Her work was complete"], answer: 2, explain: "The article says there is still a long way to go.", level: 3 },
      { q: "Tanya, a girl in a small town, wants to study physics though people say it is for boys. Which part of the lesson can inspire her?", options: ["ISRO’s budget","Bibha’s persistence against social expectations","Cosmic ray details","Chandrayaan dates"], answer: 1, explain: "Bibha overcame such expectations.", level: 3 },
      { q: "A school names its science lab after a woman scientist who received no award in her lifetime. Which idea from the lesson does this reflect?", options: ["Awards do not matter","Labs need names","Only men deserve credit","Late but fitting recognition of a pioneer"], answer: 3, explain: "Bibha was honoured later, with a star and a chair.", level: 3 }
