      { q: "Case: Riya’s school held a ‘Women in Science’ week. She read about Bibha Chowdhuri and prepared a poster titled ‘A Star Named Bibha’. Her classmates asked why she chose it. She said, ‘Because she shows that curiosity has no gender.’ (i) Why is the title suitable? (ii) Which quality of Bibha does Riya admire? (iii) What can students learn?", a: "(i) A star was named ‘Bibha’ in her honour, meaning beam of light. (ii) Her persistence and curiosity despite barriers. (iii) Anyone can pursue science with effort, and we should recognise unsung pioneers.", marks: 4, type: "case" }
